> Why not just drop a scroll of scare monster? It'll have a very similar 
> effect with most monsters (they won't attack you HtH, but they will 
> attack at range), so would this really add that much?

It will add five things: 

1.  It allows you to move.  Remember, the field is centered on you and
moves as you do.  With a scroll of scare monster, you're safe -- but
you can't move off that square.   Further, there is a non-zero chance
your scroll will go POOF if you pick it up, and you're dead. With a
scroll of repulsion, you can physically push the bad guys away and
make a run for the exit.

2. It gives you breathing room.  Unless you're surrounded by
undiggable space e.g. Sokoban, even if the field disappears next turn,
you have a clear space around you, giving you freedom to make a run
for the exit, use a polearm, push away a mind flayer or what not.

3. As mentioned elsewhere, you can attack people with it, and it can
be also used as an impromptu way to make a hole in a wall if you need
one and are short of some means of digging.

4.  The cursed version can be used for a quick escape.  Yes, it'll
hurt -- but if you've got the HP and you need to move suddenly away
from where you are, it's just the ticket.

5.  It adds people going through walls and being thrown around like
china dolls, which to me by itself is worth the price of admission :).
 I'm the sort who, in fantasy at least, never does things the quiet,
unobtrusive way if there's possibly a way to do it with a bang :).

